      "content": "wait, i think you might have mixed up dc and ac there? i thought in dc the capacitor eventually blocks the current once it's fully charged, so it acts like an open circuit, not a short. and what do you mean by it acting 'inductive' in ac? can you clarify that part and maybe show me an example of how the reactance changes if i change the frequency?",
